// Regression case for commit fc46e9db: `\*` is NOT a valid escape in a plain
// string literal (it is meaningful only inside a `like` pattern), so Cedar
// rejects `"a\*b"` with `the input \* is not a valid escape`.
//
// Before the fix, Dogwood's hand-rolled decode_string listed `\*` among its
// accepted escapes and decoded it to `*`, so this policy parsed and validated
// cleanly against a real schema — a silent divergence from Cedar, which
// confines `\*` to `like` patterns. The schema below supplies a real `Read`
// action so this case is rejected ONLY by the escape check: on the pre-fix
// parser it is accepted (the bug); after the fix it is a parse error.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when { context.input.document == "a\*b" };
